Permission allow rule (../../../.claude/settings.json): Write(.claude/**) is not matched by file permission checks — only Edit(path) rules are. Use Edit(.claude/**) instead (Edit rules cover all file-editing tools).
Two things are missing: the group never exposes `aria-invalid`/`aria-required`, and the invalid state is driven off `error` alone — so a `valueMissing` validity (no consumer message) is silent to AT and never reaches the children.

```js
  // "valid" is the only non-invalid state; anything else means the group is invalid
  get isInvalid() {
    return Boolean(this.validity) && this.validity !== 'valid';
  }

  updated(changedProperties) {
    // validity is authoritative, so react to it too -- `error` alone misses valueMissing
    if (changedProperties.has('error') || changedProperties.has('validity')) {
      const invalid = this.isInvalid;

      this.items.forEach((el) => {
        // existing behaviour: mirror the error attribute onto each child
        if (this.error) el.setAttribute('error', '');
        else el.removeAttribute('error');

        // each radio is individually focusable, so it carries the state itself
        if (invalid) el.setAttribute('aria-invalid', 'true');
        else el.removeAttribute('aria-invalid');
      });
    }
  }

  render() {
    const invalid = this.isInvalid;

    return html`
      <fieldset
        role="radiogroup"
        aria-required="${this.required ? 'true' : 'false'}"
        aria-invalid="${invalid ? 'true' : 'false'}"
        aria-describedby="${ifDefined(this.error ? 'error-message' : undefined)}">
        <legend><slot name="legend"></slot></legend>
        <slot></slot>
        ${this.error
          ? html`<p id="error-message" role="alert">${this.error}</p>`
          : nothing}
      </fieldset>
    `;
  }
```

Add `import { ifDefined } from 'lit/directives/if-defined.js';`.

What changed and why:

- **`aria-invalid` on the `fieldset`** — the invalid state is now announced when the group is reached, and it's derived from `validity`, not `error`, so `valueMissing` counts.
- **`aria-invalid` on each child** — radios are the focusable elements; a SR user arrowing between options after the initial group announcement otherwise gets nothing. Reads `validity`, so it no longer depends on a consumer-supplied `error` string.
- **`aria-describedby` → the message** — associates the text with the group so it's read on focus, not only at the moment it appears.
- **`updated()` now also keys on `validity`** — previously, `validity` flipping to `valueMissing` re-rendered but never touched the children.
- **Dropped `aria-live="assertive"`** — `role="alert"` already implies it; the pair causes duplicate announcements in some SR/browser combinations.

One gap this doesn't close, since it needs a product decision: when `validity === 'valueMissing'` and no `error` is set, the group reports `aria-invalid="true"` with no message explaining why. Either have `valueMissing` fall back to a default string ("Select an option") rendered in the same `<p>`, or require consumers to set `error` alongside it.
